  "title": "Service availability below 100% during traffic spike",
  "description": "A sudden traffic increase exceeds current replica/connection capacity: request rate reached 2310rpm vs a ~1400rpm baseline, active connections hit 498/500, HTTP 503s rose to 2.1%, p95 latency 4.9s and availability dropped to 98.7% while HPA scaling lagged behind (6 replicas now, 10 desired). Reduced availability, elevated traffic, connection saturation and delayed scaling are directly observed; it is not proven that a restart is required or that timeouts alone would have prevented this.",
